Answer the MiscTA message the modem sends when a call ends.

The modem sends message 4 on QMI service 228 at the end of every
answered call and waits for a reply. Ignoring it starves the modem's
non-volatile storage task, and a couple of minutes later its own
watchdog kills the firmware:

  qcom-q6v5-mss fc880000.remoteproc: fatal error received:
    dog.c:1639:Watchdog detects task starvation of nve

The modem then reloads and re-enumerates, ModemManager loses and
refinds it, and incoming calls are refused in between.

What the message asks for is not known. If it is a write, guessing at
one would be worse than not writing, because that partition holds the
radio calibration, so this reports success and writes nothing, which
is enough to let the modem's task finish. The transaction id is read
straight from the QMI header because libqrtr's decoder rejects any TLV
it has no definition for.

--- a/qmi_ta228.qmi	2026-09-17 18:49:41.284895513 +0100
+++ b/qmi_ta228.qmi	2026-09-17 19:09:28.411491595 +0100
@@ -20,3 +20,12 @@
 	required u32 result = 1;
 	required u8 data(65535) = 16;
 } = 2;
+
+const TA228_ACK = 4;
+
+request ack_req {
+} = 4;
+
+response ack_resp {
+	required u32 result = 1;
+} = 4;
--- a/main.c	2026-09-17 18:49:40.771504820 +0100
+++ b/main.c	2026-09-17 19:09:27.720490559 +0100
@@ -33,6 +33,7 @@
 #include <stdio.h>
 #include <stdlib.h>
 #include <string.h>
+#include <endian.h>
 #include <libqrtr.h>
 
 #include "qmi_ta227.h"
@@ -315,6 +316,73 @@
